# Zealakit Chrono conventions

- `@zealakit/chrono-core` is framework-independent and has zero runtime dependencies. Never
  import React / Vue / Svelte from it.
- Adapters (`vanilla`, `react`, `vue`, `svelte`) depend on core with `workspace:^`; core depends
  on no adapter. Keep the dependency graph acyclic.
- Root entry → domain entries (`/calendar`, `/date`, `/time`, `/datetime`) → core. Respect the
  domain import graph in `plans/02-implement-business-flow.md` §2.6.
- No dependency on any UI library (`@zealakit/overlay-*`, Radix, Base UI, …) in core or the four
  adapters, and no path links to sibling repositories. Run `pnpm check:deps` and
  `pnpm check:independence`. Only the `@zealakit/chrono-picker-*` packages (plan 14) may
  list `@zealakit/overlay-<fw>`, as a peer only.
- No popup, portal, or positioning code in core or the adapters (picker packages: plan 14). No
  required global Provider.
- SSR safety: no `window` / `document` access at module init or during render.
- Do not ship CSS or a styling system. Styling is the consumer's job (`data-*`, ARIA and
  `--chrono-*` custom properties only).
- Chrono proposes changes; it never persists, fetches, or applies business rules.
- New code ships with focused tests (`pnpm test`). Do not add a second test framework.
- Do not export unimplemented APIs, placeholder components, or empty entry points.
- TypeScript only: `type` aliases, `import type`, strict mode, ESM. Files are `kebab-case`.
- Build order matters: core emits `dist` first; adapters resolve core through its package
  exports. Run `pnpm build` before `pnpm typecheck`.
- Verify with `pnpm check` before reporting work as done. Run example builds when those areas
  change.
- `examples/` are integration/smoke-test projects only. Product documentation lives only in the
  root and package READMEs (EN, VI, CN); there is no `docs/` folder.
- Load `.agents/skills/chrono/SKILL.md` before code, test, docs, or release work, and
  `.agents/skills/readme-system/SKILL.md` before touching any README. Run `pnpm readme:check`
  after README changes.
